# Vega Design Spec — Sprint 4: Dark Mode Certification + Theme Toggle

**Project:** InkOS | **Stack:** A (Next.js 16 + Supabase + Railway) | **Date:** 2026-04-17
**Sprint plan ref:** `~/.claude/plans/giggly-kindling-bee.md` Sprint 4
**Nova benchmark:** `.handoffs/nova-sprint-4-benchmark.md` — file absent, audit proceeds from codebase.

---

## Audit Findings (pre-sprint state)

### Two competing `.dark` blocks in `app/globals.css`

`globals.css` contains two separate `.dark {}` blocks:

- **Block 1** (lines 667–712): defines core semantic tokens with `oklch(11%)` background, `oklch(14.5%)` card, `oklch(22%)` border, `oklch(60%)` muted-foreground. Sidebar tokens included. No surface-elevation tokens beyond `surface-1/2`. No auth tokens. Shadow values are weak (0.2-0.4 alpha).
- **Block 2** (lines 829–899): defines a richer, separate-philosophy palette with `oklch(15%)` background, `oklch(20%)` card, `oklch(28%)` border, `oklch(65%)` muted-foreground. Has `surface-1/2/3/elevated`, KPI accent colors, `--shadow-glow-card`, `--shadow-card-hover`, `--shadow-glow-purple`, auth tokens (`--color-auth-bg/card/border`), stronger shadow alphas (0.35-0.65), and shimmer override.

**Resolution: Block 2 is authoritative.** It is more complete, uses the correct philosophy (Linear/Notion dark, not pitch-black), and adds tokens Block 1 lacks. Koda must merge the two blocks into one. Block 1 values that conflict with Block 2 are superseded by Block 2. Block 1 tokens absent from Block 2 (see Section 1 below) must be added to Block 2 before Block 1 is deleted.

### `ThemeToggle` component state

`components/shared/ThemeToggle.tsx` exists but exports only `ThemeToggle()` with no `variant` prop. It is a binary sun/moon toggle (no system option). Touch target is `size-8` (32px) — below the 44px minimum. The component is NOT currently rendered in `AppHeader` — the header has only a `DropdownMenuSub` for theme inside the user menu.

### Recharts consumers (complete inventory)

7 files consume Recharts directly:

```
components/admin/AdminDashboardClient.tsx
components/reports/AiUsageReportClient.tsx
components/reports/BookingsReportClient.tsx
components/reports/RechartsAreaChart.tsx
components/reports/RechartsBarChart.tsx
components/reports/RevenueReportClient.tsx
app/(app)/dev/design/DesignShowcase.tsx
```

`components/reports/RechartsAreaChart.tsx` and `components/reports/RechartsBarChart.tsx` are likely chart primitives that the other report files consume. All 7 must be updated to use `getChartTheme`.

### Auth layout

`app/(auth)/layout.tsx` uses two raw oklch values as inline styles:
- `bg-[oklch(96%_0.008_264)]` on the root flex container — hardcoded light background that will not adapt to dark.
- `style={{ background: 'oklch(52% 0.24 292)' }}` on the left brand panel — this is the brand purple and is intentionally fixed.

The right panel form card correctly uses `bg-card border-border` (token-based). The outer flex container background must be migrated to `var(--color-background)`.

### `book/layout.tsx`

Already uses `var(--booking-bg, hsl(var(--background)))` — theme-aware by default. No changes needed unless `--booking-bg` is never set (in which case it falls through to `--background` correctly). No action required.

---

## Section 1 — Dark Palette Refinement

### Merge resolution table

The table below covers every semantic token. "Use" = keep the Block 2 value. "Add" = token missing from Block 2 (was only in Block 1) — must be appended. "No change" = Block 1 and Block 2 agree or Block 2 is clearly better.

| Token | Block 1 value | Block 2 value | Decision | Contrast note |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `--color-background` | `oklch(11% 0.012 264)` | `oklch(15% 0.01 264)` | **Use Block 2** | Warmer slate, matches Linear/Notion dark |
| `--color-foreground` | `oklch(95% 0.008 264)` | `oklch(95% 0.005 264)` | **Use Block 2** | Both pass 4.5:1 on background |
| `--color-card` | `oklch(14.5% 0.014 264)` | `oklch(20% 0.015 264)` | **Use Block 2** | Block 2 provides clear 5-point L separation from background; Block 1's 3.5-point gap is too subtle |
| `--color-card-foreground` | `oklch(95% 0.008 264)` | implied same as `--color-foreground` | **Use Block 2** `oklch(95% 0.005 264)` | |
| `--color-popover` | `oklch(14.5% 0.014 264)` | `oklch(20% 0.015 264)` | **Use Block 2** | Same rationale as card |
| `--color-popover-foreground` | `oklch(95% 0.008 264)` | `oklch(95% 0.005 264)` | **Use Block 2** | |
| `--color-primary` | `oklch(65% 0.24 292)` | `oklch(65% 0.24 292)` | **No change** | WCAG AA: L65 on L15 background ≈ 5.8:1. Passes. |
| `--color-primary-foreground` | `oklch(10% 0.01 292)` | `oklch(99% 0 0)` | **Use Block 2 (`oklch(99% 0 0)`)** | White on purple L65 is cleaner; dark foreground on purple would fail at smaller sizes |
| `--color-secondary` | `oklch(20% 0.02 292)` | `oklch(24% 0.015 264)` | **Use Block 2** | Neutral secondary is safer than purple-tinted |
| `--color-secondary-foreground` | `oklch(85% 0.04 292)` | `oklch(88% 0.01 264)` | **Use Block 2** | |
| `--color-muted` | `oklch(18% 0.015 264)` | `oklch(22% 0.01 264)` | **Use Block 2** | Slightly lighter muted creates better disabled-input differentiation |
| `--color-muted-foreground` | `oklch(60% 0.02 264)` | `oklch(65% 0.015 264)` | **Use Block 2 — and raise to `oklch(66% 0.015 264)`** | At L60 on L15 background = approx 3.8:1 (fails AA for body text, passes for large/UI). At L65 = approx 4.6:1 (passes AA for body). At L66 = safe floor. Muted foreground is used on form helper text, table secondary text, placeholder — all at 14px (body), so 4.5:1 required. |
| `--color-accent` | `oklch(20% 0.04 292)` | `oklch(25% 0.035 292)` | **Use Block 2** | Subtle purple tint hover states |
| `--color-accent-foreground` | `oklch(80% 0.06 292)` | `oklch(78% 0.14 292)` | **Use Block 2** | Higher chroma reads as active accent text |
| `--color-destructive` | `oklch(62% 0.22 27)` | `oklch(58% 0.22 27)` | **Use `oklch(62% 0.22 27)` (Block 1 value)** | L62 on L15 background ≈ 4.7:1. L58 ≈ 4.1:1 (marginal). Use L62. |
| `--color-destructive-foreground` | `oklch(99% 0 0)` | `oklch(99% 0 0)` | **No change** | |
| `--color-border` | `oklch(22% 0.015 264)` | `oklch(28% 0.02 264)` | **Use Block 2** | L28 is more visible on L15 background without being loud. L22 is nearly invisible. |
| `--color-input` | `oklch(22% 0.015 264)` | `oklch(22% 0.015 264)` (implicit) | **Keep `oklch(22% 0.015 264)`** | Input borders match Block 1; slightly recessed from general border is intentional |
| `--color-ring` | `oklch(65% 0.24 292)` | `oklch(65% 0.24 292)` | **No change** | L65 purple on L15 dark bg ≈ 5.8:1. Focus ring passes 3:1 (UI). |
| `--color-success` | `oklch(62% 0.18 145)` | implicit (Block 1 sets in separate dark status block) | **Keep `oklch(62% 0.18 145)`** | L62 green on L15 bg ≈ 5.1:1. Passes. |
| `--color-success-bg` | `oklch(20% 0.06 145)` | — | **Keep** | |
| `--color-success-foreground` | `oklch(82% 0.12 145)` | — | **Keep** | |
| `--color-warning` | `oklch(72% 0.16 72)` | — | **Keep** | L72 amber on L15 ≈ 7.1:1. Passes. |
| `--color-warning-bg` | `oklch(22% 0.07 72)` | — | **Keep** | |
| `--color-warning-foreground` | `oklch(86% 0.12 72)` | — | **Keep** | |
| `--color-page-bg` | `oklch(11% 0.012 264)` | `oklch(14% 0.01 264)` | **Use Block 2** | Slightly darker than background to give depth under sidebar |
| `--color-header-bg` | `oklch(14.5% 0.014 264)` | `oklch(16% 0.01 264 / 0.97)` | **Use Block 2** | Frosted glass effect on scroll |
| `--color-surface-1` | `oklch(14.5% 0.014 264)` | `oklch(20% 0.015 264)` | **Use Block 2** | |
| `--color-surface-2` | `oklch(17% 0.016 264)` | `oklch(24% 0.012 264)` | **Use Block 2** | |
| `--color-surface-3` | absent from Block 1 | `oklch(28% 0.01 264)` | **Add (Block 2)** | |
| `--color-surface-elevated` | absent from Block 1 | `oklch(30% 0.015 264)` | **Add (Block 2)** | Modals, command palette |

### Shadow audit for dark mode

Current Block 2 shadows:

| Token | Block 2 value | Assessment | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| `--shadow-soft` | `0 1px 3px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.2), 0 1px 2px -1px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.15)` | Too weak — on L15 background, 0.2 alpha barely registers | **Raise to 0.3 / 0.22** |
| `--shadow-card` | `0 1px 4px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.25), 0 2px 8px -2px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.2)` | Acceptable | **No change** |
| `--shadow-soft-md` | `0 4px 12px -2px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.3), 0 2px 6px -2px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.2)` | Acceptable | **No change** |
| `--shadow-lift` | absent from Block 2 | Missing — used by command palette, toasts | **Add: `0 8px 24px -4px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.55), 0 4px 10px -2px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.35)`** |
| `--shadow-overlay` | absent from Block 2 | Missing — used by modals/dialogs | **Add: `0 24px 64px -12px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.75), 0 8px 24px -4px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.50)`** |
| `--shadow-card-hover` | `0 8px 25px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.35), 0 0 0 1px oklch(65% 0.24 292 / 0.2), inset 0 1px 0 oklch(100% 0 0 / 0.05)` | Good — includes purple border accent and top highlight | **No change** |
| `--shadow-glow-card` | `0 1px 3px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.2), 0 0 0 1px oklch(28% 0.02 264 / 0.6), inset 0 1px 0 oklch(100% 0 0 / 0.04)` | Good — subtle card border glow | **No change** |

### Final merged `.dark` block — exact output for Koda

Koda replaces both existing `.dark {}` blocks with this single block. No other changes to `globals.css`:

```css
