## Section 3 — `<ThemeToggle>` Component

**File:** `components/shared/ThemeToggle.tsx`

The existing file exports a single `ThemeToggle()` function (no variant). It is completely replaced with a two-variant component.

### Variant: `icon`

- Size: `h-9 w-9` (36px — minimum for desktop, acceptable given header density; not the 44px mobile floor because this is a desktop-primary element. Mobile gets the system preference toggle in settings.)
- Icon: `Sun` (in dark mode — clicking sets light) / `Moon` (in light mode — clicking sets dark). The icon that is shown represents the mode you will switch TO, following industry standard (Vercel, Linear pattern).
- Tooltip: "Switch to light mode" / "Switch to dark mode"
- No spin animation. `transition-colors` only. Respects `prefers-reduced-motion` automatically via the global `button` transition rule.
- On `system` theme: `resolvedTheme` determines which icon shows; clicking always sets an explicit `'light'` or `'dark'`, removing system preference until user resets.

### Variant: `segmented`

- Width: `w-full max-w-[240px]`
- 3 buttons inside a single rounded container: **Light** / **System** / **Dark**
- Container: `inline-flex items-center gap-0 rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted p-0.5`
- Each button: `flex h-8 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md px-3 text-[13px] font-medium text-muted-foreground transition-colors`
- Active button: `bg-background text-foreground shadow-[var(--shadow-soft)]`
- Icons: `Sun` (14px) before "Light", `SunMoon` (14px) before "System", `Moon` (14px) before "Dark"
- `aria-pressed="true"` on the active button
- Clicking "System" calls `setTheme('system')` — this clears the persisted preference and returns control to `prefers-color-scheme`.

### Component code

```tsx
'use client'

import { Moon, Sun, SunMoon } from 'lucide-react'
import { useTheme } from 'next-themes'
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'
import { Tooltip, TooltipContent, TooltipTrigger } from '@/components/ui/tooltip'
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils'

interface ThemeToggleProps {
  variant?: 'icon' | 'segmented'
  className?: string
}

export function ThemeToggle({ variant = 'icon', className }: ThemeToggleProps) {
  const { theme, resolvedTheme, setTheme } = useTheme()

  if (variant === 'segmented') {
    const options = [
      { value: 'light',  label: 'Light',  Icon: Sun    },
      { value: 'system', label: 'System', Icon: SunMoon },
      { value: 'dark',   label: 'Dark',   Icon: Moon   },
    ] as const
    return (
      <div
        role="group"
        aria-label="Color theme"
        className={cn(
          'inline-flex items-center gap-0 rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted p-0.5',
          className,
        )}
      >
        {options.map(({ value, label, Icon }) => (
          <button
            key={value}
            type="button"
            onClick={() => setTheme(value)}
            aria-pressed={theme === value}
            className={cn(
              'flex h-8 cursor-pointer items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md px-3 text-[13px] font-medium text-muted-foreground transition-colors',
              theme === value && 'bg-background text-foreground shadow-[var(--shadow-soft)]',
            )}
          >
            <Icon className="h-3.5 w-3.5" aria-hidden="true" />
            {label}
          </button>
        ))}
      </div>
    )
  }

  // icon variant
  const isDark = resolvedTheme === 'dark'
  return (
    <Tooltip>
      <TooltipTrigger asChild>
        <Button
          variant="ghost"
          size="icon"
          className={cn('h-9 w-9', className)}
          onClick={() => setTheme(isDark ? 'light' : 'dark')}
          aria-label={isDark ? 'Switch to light mode' : 'Switch to dark mode'}
        >
          {isDark
            ? <Sun className="h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true" />
            : <Moon className="h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true" />
          }
        </Button>
      </TooltipTrigger>
      <TooltipContent>
        {isDark ? 'Light mode' : 'Dark mode'}
      </TooltipContent>
    </Tooltip>
  )
}
```

### Placement in `AppHeader`

Insert `<ThemeToggle variant="icon" />` inside the right-side `div` in `components/app/sidebar/AppHeader.tsx`, between the Cmd+K pill and the avatar dropdown:

