## Section 5 — Auth Pages

**Decision: Support both modes.** Remove the hard-coded dark background from the auth layout outer container.

**Rationale:** The auth page is the first impression. A user on a system set to light mode arriving at a hard-dark auth page creates friction and a jarring contrast with the app they are about to enter. The left brand panel (purple) is always the brand panel regardless of theme — it stays purple. Only the right panel's outer background adapts.

### Changes to `app/(auth)/layout.tsx`

**Current issue:** Line 29 — `bg-[oklch(96%_0.008_264)]` hardcodes the light-mode page background on the root flex container.

**Fix:** Replace the hardcoded value with the `bg-background` semantic token:

```tsx
// BEFORE
<div className="flex min-h-svh bg-[oklch(96%_0.008_264)]">

// AFTER
<div className="flex min-h-svh bg-background">
```

The left brand panel (`style={{ background: 'oklch(52% 0.24 292)' }}`) is kept as-is. This is the brand purple. It is intentionally fixed.

The right panel form card already uses `bg-card border-border` — no change needed there.

No `--color-auth-bg` token usage is needed on the auth layout because the layout already defaults to `bg-background`. The `--color-auth-bg` token in the dark block exists for future use if a custom auth surface is needed.

